nt":592,"summary":"Little Artie Shawcross bullied classmates, insulted teachers, started fires, tortured animals, and roved the woods of New York's hardscrabble North Country with imaginary friends, talking in a high squawk. He also scored top grades, excelled in sports and shared his money and toys with the children who ridiculed him. From the second grade on, he was subjected to psychiatric examination, regularly confounding the experts. Years later, while serving in Vietnam, Arthur John Shawcross wrote bloodcurdling letters about his battlefield ordeals, then returned to Watertown to commit a string of arsons and burglaries. He served two years in prison, was paroled to his respectable parents - and murdered a boy and a girl. Back in the penitentiary, he proved as enigmatic as ever. Some counselors saw him as a Frankenstein monster, beyond hope, irredeemable.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/280517-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.058,"accessibilityScore":0.138,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"popular","score":0.22,"confidence":"low","evidence":["trade publisher signal: Delacorte Press / Penguin Random House"]},{"id":"character_driven","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"family\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":false,"publicFame":8,"criticalRenown":12,"controversy":8,"llmAffinity":42,"affinityResidual":-27.24,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.12,"criticalRenown":0.12,"controversy":0.1,"llmAffinity":0.18},"tags":{"craft":"narrative-drive","evidence":"reportage","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"displaySummary":"From the second grade on, he was subjected to psychiatric examination, regularly confounding the experts. Years later, while serving in Vietnam, Arthur John Shawcross wrote bloodcurdling letters about his battlefield ordeals, then returned to Watertown to commit a string of arsons and 